  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rwanda: Value-added Initiative to Boost Employment (VIBE) for Refugees</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Value Added Initiative to Boost Employment (VIBE) for Refugees in Rwanda supports 900 refugee youth in agricultural sectors, both those that are self-employed and part of MSMEs and cooperatives, to increase their competitiveness and participation in local and regional trade in Rwanda. The key areas of intervention are 1. Strengthen market linkages between refugee-inclusive MSMEs and businesses 2. Enhance inclusive and enabling business and market ecosystems for refugees3. Improve policy around refugee market and employment inclusion</narrative>
  </description>
